<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Catugnatus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 61 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Catugnatus was a leader of the Allobroges, a Gallic people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> valley, who led their revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 62–61 BCE. The rising followed Roman neglect of the tribe's complaints about debts and misgovernment. The governor Gaius Pomptinus crushed the Allobroges, and Catugnatus is known only from the account of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassius-dio">Cassius Dio</a>.</p></div>
